# Installation

## Prerequisites

### CUDA Toolkit (11.x or later)
Download from https://developer.nvidia.com/cuda-downloads
Follows the installer for your Linux distribution.

Verify installation:
  nvcc --version
  nvidia-smi

### CUDA Samples (for helper headers)
  git clone https://github.com/NVIDIA/cuda-samples.git /usr/local/cuda/samples

Or set SAMPLE_DIR in the Makefile to point to your local clone.

### Python 3 + Pillow (test data generation only)
  pip3 install Pillow

---

## Build

  cd <project-root>
  make

If CUDA or samples are in non-standard locations:
  make CUDA_PATH=/path/to/cuda SAMPLE_DIR=/path/to/cuda-samples

---

## Generate Test Images

  make data

Creates 120 synthetic 512x512 .pgm images in data/input/.

---

## Run

  ./run.sh            # blur+sobel on all images in data/input
  ./run.sh blur       # Gaussian blur only
  ./run.sh sobel      # Sobel edge detection only

Or directly:
  ./bin/batchImageProc --input=data/input --output=data/output --filter=all

---

## Troubleshooting

- "cannot find -lnppc"  : ensure CUDA 11+ is installed and lib64 is in LD_LIBRARY_PATH
- "helper_cuda.h not found" : set SAMPLE_DIR to your cuda-samples clone path
- Pillow missing        : pip3 install Pillow
